        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/bradwell_windmill.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>Passivhaus</title>
        <description>A wander through Manor Park might take you back in time to the Georgian era, but it&apos;s a place where Alan Budden and his colleagues are designing housing of the future. &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://www.ecodesignconsultants.co.uk/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Eco Design Consultants&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/passivhaus.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/passivhaus.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='12312192'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/passivhaus.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>Amazing Grace</title>
        <description>Why do people come from around the globe to visit this museum and then sing a hymn in the local church? Tom Jones helps us find out why. &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://cowperandnewtonmuseum.org.uk/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Cowper &amp; Newton Museum&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/cowper_newton_museum.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/cowper_newton_museum.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='30012360'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/cowper_newton_museum.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>A home for all</title>
        <description>It&apos;s a charity, a community and a popular place to have a break. I speak to Lynn Reeves to Operations Manager to find out more. &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://emmaus.org.uk/village-carlton/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Emmaus website&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/emmaus.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/emmaus.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='2743406'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/emmaus.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>Harrold Odell Park</title>
        <description>It&apos;s been called the jewel of North Bedfordshire and the Ouse Valley Way passes right through it. I meet Ed Green who shares with us how he keeps this local gem in good order. &lt;a href=&apos;https://hocp.co.uk/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Park website&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/hocp.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/harrold_odell_country_park.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='8114904'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/harrold_odell_country_park.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>A Pilgrim&apos;s Progress</title>
        <description>Between Pavenham and Bromham Mill, the Ouse Valley Way joins another walking route - The John Bunyan Trail. I met with John Pestell from the Bunyan Museum to find out more about the man and his greatest work. &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://www.bunyanmeeting.co.uk/museum&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Bunyan Museum&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/john_bunyan.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/john_bunyan.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='18048759'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/john_bunyan.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>Guru Nanak Gurdwara</title>
        <description>There&apos;s an impressive temple visible from the Ouse Valley Way. Let&apos;s go visit it and learn some lessons for people of all faiths and none. &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://www.facebook.com/GuruNanakGurdwaraBedford/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Facebook page&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/guru_nanak_temple.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/guru_nanak_gurdwara_temple.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='7122288'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/guru_nanak_gurdwara_temple.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>20th Century Preppers</title>
        <description>What would you do if an Apocalypse was imminent? Museum director, Zara Matthews, shows us what one incredible group of ladies decided to do. &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://panaceamuseum.org/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Panacea Museum&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/panacea.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/panacea.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='37009657'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/panacea.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>Remembering the R101</title>
        <description>Why did the R101&apos;s maiden flight end in tragedy? Lydia McDonald, Keeper of Social History at the Higgins, helps us find out. She also shows us why Bedford was a centre for innovation that made it the place to build airships. &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://www.thehigginsbedford.org.uk/Home.aspx&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Website&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/higgins.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/higgins.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='14438280'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/higgins.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>Paxton Pits</title>
        <description>Paxton Pits Ranger, Robyn Staddon takes us to a bird hide to descover the special things to see and hear in the nature reserve.&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://paxton-pits.org.uk/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Paxton Pits&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/paxton_pits.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/paxton_pits.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='6221649'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/paxton_pits.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>Roxton Chapel</title>
        <description>Richard Hooker shows us around a chapel that used to have a very different purpose.&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://roxtonchapel.wixsite.com/about&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Chapel Website&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/roxton_church.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/roxtonchapel.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='9226200'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/roxtonchapel.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>Warts and all</title>
        <description>Curator Stuart Orme takes us around the Cromwell Museum to learn about one of England&apos;s most consequential and controversial figures in history.&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://www.cromwellmuseum.org/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Cromwell Museum&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/cromwell_museum.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/cromwell_museum.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='36424896'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/cromwell_museum.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>Citizen Science</title>
        <description>Let&apos;s join Lucas Tatek who regularly tests the river checking for harmful bacteria at a popular paddling place. &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://greatouseways.info/join.html&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;find a citizen science group&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://www.gov.uk/report-environmental-problem&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Environment Agency&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/citizenscience.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/citizenscience.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='3688152'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/citizenscience.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>Watermills</title>
        <description>Keith Grimwade and Bridget Flannagan have done a deep dive into the history and geography of watermilling in the area and found some surprising things that will change how we see the landscape.&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://www.oxbowbooks.com/9781914427411/the-watermills-and-landscape-of-the-river-great-ouse-cambridgeshire/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Book details&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/keith_and_bridget.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/watermills.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='44509248'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/watermills.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>A lasting legacy</title>
        <description>When avid collector Herbert Norris died in 1931, he left his collection of Huntingdonshire artifacts to St Ives. Richard Carter takes us on a guided tour and shows us how people today are learning about Huntingdonshire.&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://www.norrismuseum.org.uk/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Norris Museum&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/norris.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/norris.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='17588064'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/norris.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>Building a habitat</title>
        <description>A project is underway turning quarried land into a unique reserve, based on reedbeds. Let&apos;s talk to the wardens Richard Taylor and Ian Weller to find out more. &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://www.rspb.org.uk/days-out/reserves/ouse-fen&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;RSPB Ouse Fen&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/rspb_ouse_fen.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/rspb_ouse_fen.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='21861072'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/rspb_ouse_fen.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>Keeping farming afloat</title>
        <description>The Fens are Britain&apos;s bread-basket thanks to pumping stations keeping the land drained. Volunteer Nick Sharpe shows us how Stretham Old Engine has been helping keep the country fed. &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://strethamoldengine.com/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Museum website&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/stretham.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/stretham_old_engine.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='13346903'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/stretham_old_engine.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>The art of glass</title>
        <description>Most of the churches along the Ouse Valley Way contain treasures hiding in plain sight - stained glass. Emily Allen from the Stained Glass Museum is going to help us see what we have been looking through. &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://stainedglassmuseum.com/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Museum website&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/stained_glass_museum.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/stained_glass_museum.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='14338838'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/stained_glass_museum.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>Cromwell&apos;s House</title>
        <description>An obvious place to start any visit to Ely is at the tourist information office and it comes with an added bonus - it was also Oliver Cromwell’s family home which Anna Bennett shows us around. &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://www.olivercromwellshouse.co.uk/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Website&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/cromwells_house.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/cromwells_house.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='6220392'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/cromwells_house.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
      <item>
        <title>The Gingerbread Trail</title>
        <description>Discover Downham volunteer, Kathleen Wiseman, takes us on a tour of Downham to find out why it&apos;s known as the &lt;i&gt;Gingerbread Town&lt;/i&gt;. It&apos;s also a chance to meet the dedicated volunteers who have been determined to save the artifacts and share the stories of their town. &lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&apos;https://www.discoverdownham.org.uk/&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Discover Downham&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <pubDate>Sat, 01 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <itunes:image url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/images/thumbnails/downham.jpg' />
        <enclosure url='https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/downham.mp3' type='audio/mpeg' length='22835064'/>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://greatouseways.info/assets/audio/downham.mp3</guid>
      </item>
    
